Nf6 8. O-O Bb4 9. Na4 $1 {is strong - Barden}) 8. Nxc6 dxc6 9. f4 Bb7 10. O-O
c5 11. Bf3 Be7 ({Better than} 11... b4 12. Na4 Nf6 13. c3 {Barden}) ({or} 11...
Nf6 12. e5) 12. Qe2 (12. e5 Nh6) 12... Nf6 13. e5 Nd7 14. Rad1 (14. Bxb7 Qxb7
15. f5 exf5 16. Rxf5 O-O {with a sound game - Archives (quoted by Barden)})
14... O-O 15. Ne4 Bd5 16. b3 Nb6 $2 (16... c4 $1 $11 {Barden}) 17. Qf2 Rac8 18.
Qg3 Kh8 19. f5 exf5 $2 (19... f6 {might still hold on - Barden}) 20. Nd6 Bxd6 (
20... Be6 $14 {Houdini 4 Pro}) 21. exd6 $18 Qc6 22. Rxd5 Nxd5 23. Rd1 f4 24.
Bxd5 Qxd5 25. Rxd5 fxg3 26. d7 gxh2+ 27. Kxh2 Rcd8 28. Bxc5 Kg8 29. c4 bxc4 30.
bxc4 f6 31. Bxf8 Kxf8 32. c5 {Sources: The Guardian, 13 Aug 1964; BCM, Sept
1964, p254} 1-0

